# The base map is part tracked, part generated. Levels 0-2 and the manifest are
# committed — 42 tiles and 0.35 MB — so every checkout has a correct globe without
# running docker, and the app has no absent-imagery case to handle. The iOS app
# ships level 2 from here too (its target's "Copy Natural Earth" phase). Levels 3-5
# are 17.2 MB and come from `pnpm update-imagery`.
#
# Safe to commit because the generator is reproducible: levels 0-2 come out
# byte-identical across repeated runs, process counts, and arm64 against amd64. The
# source archive is pinned by checksum (`SOURCE_SHA256`) so that stays true, and the
# depth is fixed because a shallower run would produce different pixels for these
# same levels.
NaturalEarthII/3/
NaturalEarthII/4/
NaturalEarthII/5/
